 He lived at Haran in Mesopotamia. His sister Rebekah was Isaac’s wife (Gen. 24).","verses":46,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[18,25]},{"id":"zilpah_3081","name":"Zilpah","also":"","summary":"Drooping, Leah’s handmaid, and the mother of Gad and Asher (Gen. 30:9-13).","verses":7,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[19,21]},{"id":"rachel_2386","name":"Rachel","also":"Rahel","summary":"Ewe, “the daughter”, “the somewhat petulant, peevish, and self-willed though beautiful younger daughter” of Laban, and one of Jacob’s wives (Gen. 29:6, 28).","verses":45,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[19,22,25]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[20]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[20]},{"id":"asenath_335","name":"Asenath","also":"","summary":"An Egyptian name, meaning “gift of the sun-god”, daughter of Potipherah, priest of On or Heliopolis, wife of Joseph (Gen. 41:45).","verses":3,"father":"Poti-pherah","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"poti-pherah_2369","name":"Poti-pherah","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"bela_436","name":"Bela","also":"Belah","summary":"The eldest son of Benjamin (Num. 26:38; “Belah,” Gen. 46:21).","verses":7,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"ashbel_336","name":"Ashbel","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"becher_423","name":"Becher","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"gera_1298","name":"Gera","also":"","summary":"The father of Ehud the judge (Judg. 3:15).","verses":3,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"huram_1569","name":"Huram","also":"Hupham, Huppim","summary":"Generally “Huram,” one of the sons of Bela (1 Chr. 8:5).","verses":3,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"shupham_2115","name":"Shupham","also":"Shephuphan, Muppim","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"ehi_1038","name":"Ehi","also":"Aharah","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"nohah_2120","name":"Nohah","also":"Naaman","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"rapha_2447","name":"Rapha","also":"Rosh","summary":"A Benjamite, the son of Binea (1 Chr. 8:2, 37), a descendant of Saul.","verses":2,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"ard_293","name":"Ard","also":"","summary":"One that commands.","verses":1,"father":"Benjamin","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[23]},{"id":"hushim_1579","name":"Hushim","also":"Shuham","summary":"Son of Dan.","verses":2,"father":"Dan","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[24]},{"id":"guni_1330","name":"Guni","also":"","summary":"Son of Naphtali.","verses":3,"father":"Naphtali","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"jahzeel_706","name":"Jahzeel","also":"Jahziel","summary":"Allotted by God, the first of the sons of Naphtali (Gen. 46:24).","verses":3,"father":"Naphtali","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"jezer_1606","name":"Jezer","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Naphtali","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"shillem_2677","name":"Shillem","also":"Shallum","summary":"1 Chr. 7:13.","verses":3,"father":"Naphtali","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"bilhah_502","name":"Bilhah","also":"","summary":"Faltering; bashful, Rachel’s handmaid, whom she gave to Jacob (Gen. 29:29). She was the mother of Dan and Naphtali (Gen. 30:3-8). Reuben was cursed by his father for committing adultry with her (35:22; 49:4).","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[1,5]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[3,4,6,7,8,20,26,27]},{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[6,10,12,31]},{"id":"paddan-aram_916","name":"Paddan-aram","kind":"","lat":36.86386,"lon":39.0322,"summary":"The plain of Aram, or the plain of the highlands, (Gen. 25:20; 28:2, 5-7; 31:18, etc.), commonly regarded as the district of Mesopotamia lying around Haran.","verses":10,"v":[15]},{"id":"on_908","name":"On","kind":"City","lat":30.10809,"lon":31.33822,"summary":"Light; the sun, (Gen. 41:45, 50), the great seat of sun-worship, called also Bethshemesh (Jer. 43:13) and Aven (Ezek. 30:17), stood on the east bank of the Nile, a few miles north of Memphis, and near Cairo, in the north-east.","verses":4,"v":[20]},{"id":"goshen_490","name":"Goshen","kind":"Region","lat":30.7285,"lon":31.80469,"summary":"A district in Egypt where Jacob and his family settled, and in which they remained till the Exodus (Gen. 45:10; 46:28, 29, 31, etc.). It is called “the land of Goshen” (47:27), and also simply “Goshen” (46:28), and “the land of Rameses” (47:11; Ex. 12:37), for the towns Pithom and Rameses lay within its borders; also Zoan or Tanis (Ps. 78:12).","verses":11,"v":[28,29,34]}],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_job_107","title":"Birth of Job","year":-1720,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 46:13. People: Job.","v":[13]},{"id":"lifetime_of_job_108","title":"Lifetime of Job","year":-1720,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 46:13 – Job 42:17. People: Job. Lasted about 140 years.","v":[13]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3478,3478,5265,5265,3605,3605,834,0,0,935,935,935,935,884,884,2076,2076,2077,430,430,430,1,1,1,3327],[3915,3915,3915,430,559,3478,3478,4759,4759,4759,3290,3290,559,559,2009,2009,2009,559,559],[595,410,410,559,559,430,430,1,1,1,408,408,3372,3372,3381,3381,3381,4714,4714,3588,7760,7760,7760,1419,1419,1419,1419,1471,8033],[595,3381,3381,3381,5973,4714,4714,4714,595,595,1571,1571,5927,5927,5927,3130,3130,3027,3027,7896,7896,5869,5869],[3290,3290,6965,884,884,1121,1121,1121,3478,3478,5375,1,1,3290,5699,5699,5699,6547,7971,7971,5375,5375,5375,2945,2945,2945,2945,802,802],[3947,3947,3947,4735,4735,7399,7399,7408,7408,7408,776,776,776,3667,3667,3290,3290,3605,3605,2233,2233,935,4714,4714],[935,935,854,854,4714,4714,1121,1121,1121,1121,1323,1323,1323,1323,1323,2233,2233],[428,428,8034,8034,8034,1121,1121,1121,3478,3478,3290,1121,1121,1121,935,935,4714,4714,7205,3290,1060],[1121,1121,7205,7205,2585,6396,2696,3756,3756],[1121,1121,8095,8095,3223,3226,161,3199,6714,7586,7586,1121,1121,3669,3669,3669,3669],[1121,112